async function request(path:string,method='GET',value?:any,expected=200) {const response=await fetch(origin+path,{method,headers:value instanceof FormData?undefined:value!==undefined?{'Content-Type':'application/json'}:undefined,body:value===undefined?undefined:value instanceof FormData?value:JSON.stringify(value)});const text=await response.text();let data:any;try{data=JSON.parse(text);}catch{data=text;}if(response.status!==expected)throw new Error(`${method} ${path}: expected ${expected}, got ${response.status}: ${typeof data==='object'?JSON.stringify({error:data.error,message:data.message,runId:data.detail?.run?.id,phase:data.detail?.phase,events:data.detail?.run?.events}):text.slice(0,200)}`);return data;}
function assert(value:any,message:string){if(!value)throw new Error(message);}
async function check(id:string,goal:string,run:()=>Promise<any>){const start=Date.now();try{const evidence=await run();checkpoints.push({id,goal,status:'PASS',elapsedMs:Date.now()-start,evidence});console.log(`PASS ${id} ${goal}`);}catch(e){checkpoints.push({id,goal,status:'FAIL',elapsedMs:Date.now()-start,error:String(e)});console.log(`FAIL ${id} ${String(e)}`);throw e;}finally{writeFileSync(join(output,'manifest.json'),JSON.stringify(report,null,2));}}
